{% import 'macros/text.j2' as text %}
{% import 'macros/durations.j2' as durations %}
{#- The choices are the community's consent texts: the accesses (offers that require no
    other) first, then the uses, each in the consent texts' order. -#}
{% set ns = namespace(access=[], uses=[]) %}
{% for id in consent_texts.texts %}
{% if offers_by_id[id].get('requires_offers') %}{% set ns.uses = ns.uses + [id] %}{% else %}{% set ns.access = ns.access + [id] %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set choices = ns.access + ns.uses %}
{% set receivers = [] %}
{% for id in ns.access %}
{% set _ = receivers.append(party_by_alias[offers_by_id[id].recipients.recipient].short) %}
{% endfor %}
{% set platform_choices = [] %}
{% for id in choices if party_by_alias[offers_by_id[id].recipients.recipient] is sameas platform %}
{% set _ = platform_choices.append('`' ~ id ~ '`') %}
{% endfor %}
{% set first = offers_by_id[choices[0]] %}
{% macro recipient(id) %}{{ party_by_alias[offers_by_id[id].recipients.recipient].short }}{% endmacro %}
{#- The choices that require an access, in the offers' order, by id. -#}
{% macro dependents(access) %}
{%- set d = namespace(ids=[]) -%}
{%- for offer in offers if offer.id in choices and access.id in (offer.get('requires_offers') or []) -%}
{%- set d.ids = d.ids + ['`' ~ offer.id ~ '`'] -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ text.join(d.ids, 'en') }} {{ 'depend' if d.ids | length > 1 else 'depends' }} on it
{%- endmacro %}
{#- What each choice is for, by purpose. -#}
{% macro purpose(offer) %}
{%- set r = party_by_alias[offer.recipients.recipient] -%}
{%- if offer.purpose == 'MeterDataRelease' and r.kind == 'rec' -%}
{{ dso.short }} releases the member's readings to {{ r.short }}. {{ dependents(offer) }}
{%- elif offer.purpose == 'MeterDataRelease' -%}
{{ dso.short }} makes the member's readings available to {{ r.short }}. {{ dependents(offer) }}
{%- elif offer.purpose == 'FlexibilityResearch' -%}
The community's flexibility pilot in the {{ project.name }} project: estimating when consumption could be shifted, and assessing feasibility and members' participation
{%- elif offer.purpose == 'IncentiveEstimation' -%}
An estimate, for information only, of the member's shared-energy incentive ahead of GSE's official calculation, compared with that calculation once {{ r.short }} receives it
{%- elif offer.purpose == 'EnergyForecasting' -%}
{{ text.poss(r.short) }} own research and the training of energy forecasting models, including foundation models. The readings reach {{ r.short }} from {{ dso.short }} directly or through {{ rec.short }}
{%- else -%}{{ no_wording_for_purpose[offer.purpose] }}
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
---
document: {{ doc.template }}
rec: {{ rec.key }}
status: {{ doc.status }}
version: "{{ doc.version }}"
lang: {{ doc.lang }}
consent_texts: "{{ consent_texts.texts.values() | map(attribute='version') | unique | join(', ') }}"
offers: [{{ choices | join(', ') }}]
---

# Member meter data sharing agreement

**Between {{ text.join([rec.short, dso.short, platform.short], 'en') }} — version {{ doc.version }}**

## 1. Parties

| Party | Details | Role under this agreement |
|---|---|---|
| **{{ rec.name }}** ("{{ rec.short }}") | {{ rec.registered_office }}, {{ rec.country[doc.lang] }}; {% if rec.vat == rec.tax_code %}tax code and VAT {{ rec.tax_code }}{% else %}tax code {{ rec.tax_code }}; VAT {{ rec.vat }}{% endif %}; PEC {{ rec.pec }}; represented by {{ rec.representative }} | Independent controller for the purposes it pursues (§4). It is the renewable energy community and collects its members' decisions |
| **{{ dso.name }}** ("{{ dso.short }}") | {{ dso.registered_office }}; tax code {{ dso.tax_code }}; PEC {{ dso.pec }}; represented by {{ dso.representative }} | Independent controller of the release. It operates the members' meters and holds their readings |
| **{{ platform.name }}** ("{{ platform.short }}") | {{ platform.registered_office }}; tax code {{ platform.tax_code }}; PEC {{ platform.pec }}; represented by {{ platform.representative }} | Independent controller for its own research and model training (§4). Processor of {{ rec.short }} for operating the community's digital platform, and processor of {{ dso.short }} for operating its dataspace connector (§7) |

{% call text.wrap() %}
The parties are partners in the {{ project.name }} project, funded by the European Union under the
{{ project.programme }} programme, grant agreement No. {{ project.grant_agreement }}. Each party's participation in
the dataspace is governed by the dataspace participation agreement it has accepted. This
agreement adds the terms of the member meter data flow.
{% endcall %}

## 2. Purpose

{% call text.wrap() %}
This agreement lets the members of {{ text.poss(rec.short) }} renewable energy community decide
whether {{ dso.short }} releases the readings of their supply point, and whether
{{ text.join(receivers, 'en') }} use them for the purposes listed in §4. It governs each step of
that flow.
{% endcall %}

The agreement does not cover settlement with GSE, any ARERA procedure, or flexibility
contracting.

## 3. The data

{% call text.wrap('- ') %}
**Supply point code (POD)** referring to the membership of each member who has
consented. {{ rec.short }} validates it when activating the member. If it was declared
wrongly, {{ rec.short }} corrects it and records the correction as a revision.
{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('- ') %}
**Meter readings** of that POD: energy drawn from and fed into the grid, in {{ durations.span(first.resolution, 'en', true) }}
intervals, for the **{{ durations.before(first.coverage.retrospective, 'en') }} and the {{ durations.after(first.coverage.prospective, 'en') }}** the member's consent. They
are supplied in {{ text.poss(dso.short) }} {{ dso.meter_export_format }} export format, without contract details.
{% endcall %}

No member's name, contact details or tax code is disclosed under this agreement.

## 4. Consent and purposes

Each purpose rests on the member's consent. The consent is:

- asked separately for each recipient and purpose;
- never a condition of membership;
- open to withdrawal at any time.

Before deciding, the member reads version {{ consent_texts.texts.values() | map(attribute='version') | unique | join(', ') }} of the text of each choice.

| Choice | Recipient | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% for id in choices %}
| `{{ id }}` | {{ recipient(id) }} | {{ purpose(offers_by_id[id]) }} |
{% endfor %}

{% call text.wrap() %}
Each recipient keeps member-level readings for **up to {{ durations.span(first.retention, 'en') }}** from receipt, as each
choice declares.
{% endcall %}

{% for id in choices if offers_by_id[id].purpose == 'IncentiveEstimation' %}
{% call text.wrap() %}
GSE's calculation, used for the comparison in `{{ id }}`, is data {{ rec.short }}
receives from GSE as the referent of its configuration. It is not disclosed under this
agreement.
{% endcall %}
{% endfor %}

## 5. How the data moves

1. **Decision.**
{% call text.wrap('   - ') %}
{{ rec.short }} asks the member: in its onboarding form for new members, and in the
community app for existing members.
{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('   - ') %}
It records each decision and each withdrawal at {{ text.poss(dso.short) }} dataspace
connector, acting as the collector, and passes the member's POD with the decision.
{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('2. ') %}
**Release.** {{ dso.short }} serves readings through its own connector. It serves
only the PODs whose release consent is current, and only within the period in §3.
{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('3. ') %}
**Use.** {{ text.join(receivers, 'en') }} each obtain the readings through their own
connector, under the choice that names them. They use the readings only for that
choice's purpose.
{% endcall %}

{% call text.wrap() %}
**{{ dso.short }} can read the consent record at its own connector.**
{% endcall %}

- **What it sees:** for each choice it releases under, which PODs have a current release
  consent and since when, and the history of every authorisation and withdrawal.
- **What it does not see:** only the POD is shown, not the member's name, identity or
  any other consent of theirs.
{% call text.wrap('- ') %}
**What it is for:** the record is what its connector enforces. {{ dso.short }} can
therefore check and demonstrate that it releases only what step 2 allows.
{% endcall %}

{% call text.wrap() %}
No member-level list is sent to {{ dso.short }}, and no member-level readings are
released under this agreement, until the connector channel in step 1 is in operation.
How the data travels is governed by this agreement, not by the consent text, so changing
the channel does not invalidate any consent.
{% endcall %}

Every step is recorded in the dataspace's provenance record:

- each consent given and each withdrawal;
- each disclosure;
- each ingestion.

## 6. Where the data is processed

{% call text.wrap() %}
The platform runs on {{ providers.hosting.brand }} infrastructure in the European Union, and on
{{ text.poss(platform.short) }} own infrastructure in {{ platform.city }}, {{ platform.country[doc.lang] }}. The member-level data covered by this
agreement is processed only in the European Economic Area and is not transferred outside
it.
{% endcall %}

## 7. {{ platform.short }} as processor

{% call text.wrap() %}
{{ platform.short }} operates two services as a processor:
{% endcall %}

{% call text.wrap('- ', 86) %}
the community's digital platform (onboarding, community app, dataspace connector),
on {{ text.poss(rec.short) }} documented instructions;
{% endcall %}
{% call text.wrap('- ') %}
{{ text.poss(dso.short) }} dataspace connector and its consent record, on {{ text.poss(dso.short) }}
documented instructions.
{% endcall %}

Each service is governed by a separate data processing agreement under Article 28 GDPR.

{% call text.wrap() %}
{{ platform.short }} keeps its own research and model training, for which it is a controller,
separate from both services. It uses for that research only the readings it receives
under {{ text.join(platform_choices, 'en') }}.
{% endcall %}

## 8. Obligations of every party

- **Purpose and consent:** process the data only for the purpose of the choice that
  names the party, and only while the member's consent is current.
- **Withdrawal:**
  - Releases stop at once. The connector refuses the member's readings from the moment
    the withdrawal is recorded.
  - Within **7 days**, the member is left out of every export and every new processing.
  - Readings already received are kept no longer than the retention in §4. They are
    erased earlier if the member asks, within one month of the request (Articles 12(3)
    and 17 GDPR).
  - **Models already trained** with the member's readings are **not retrained**. The
    member is told so before consenting.
- **Retention:** keep no member-level data beyond the retention in §4.
- **No onward disclosure:** disclose member-level data to no one other than the three
  parties and their processors.
- **Security:** apply technical and organisational measures appropriate to energy
  consumption data, which can reveal household behaviour.
- **Assistance:** assist the other parties with data-subject requests and with
  personal-data breaches. Notify the others of a breach affecting data under this
  agreement within 48 hours of becoming aware of it.

## 9. Obligations of each party

- **{{ rec.short }}:**
  - validate each member in person before activation;
  - ask for consent without conditioning membership on it;
  - record decisions and withdrawals faithfully and pass them on without delay;
  - provide the members' information notice.
- **{{ dso.short }}:**
  - release readings only for consenting members' PODs and only within the period in §3;
  - stop releasing a POD once its consent is withdrawn;
  - use the consent record at its connector (§5) only to perform and demonstrate the
    release.
- **{{ platform.short }}:**
  - operate the services in §7 only on the documented instructions of the party
    concerned;
  - keep its own research and model training separate from that operation;
  - exclude a withdrawn member's readings from every new training run.

## 10. Term and changes

{% call text.wrap() %}
This agreement runs for the duration of the {{ project.name }} pilot and ends with it. When it ends,
each party stops receiving readings under this agreement. It keeps those already
received no longer than the retention in §4.
{% endcall %}

Changes work as follows:

- **A change to a consent text** is a new version of that choice. The member must decide
  again.
- **A change to this agreement** is a new version, signed by all three parties.

## 11. Data management plan

The project's data management plan refers to this agreement for the member meter data
flow.

## 12. Liability, law and disputes

- Each party is liable for its own processing, as provided by Article 82 GDPR.
- This agreement is governed by Italian law.
{% call text.wrap('- ') %}
The courts of {{ rec.forum[doc.lang] }} have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from it.
{% endcall %}

